        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): hide internal Code Mode wait progress",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCode Mode exposes an internal `wait` control so the model can resume suspended JavaScript runs. Channel progress treated that control like ordinary work, producing repeated `Wait` cards between real tool operations.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd invocation-specific channel-progress metadata to agent tool lifecycle events. The Code Mode `wait` control opts out of transient channel progress, while telemetry and lifecycle accounting remain intact. Synthetic catalog calls propagate metadata from their concrete tool instance, so an unrelated catalog or plugin tool also named `wait` stays visible.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDiscord and other channel progress UIs no longer show internal Code Mode `Wait` rows. Real operations such as `exec` and catalog tools continue to appear normally.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused Vitest: 5 files, 474 tests passed across unit, agent, and auto-reply shards.\n- `pnpm check:changed` passed remotely for core and core-test lanes, including typechecks, all core lint shards, import-cycle checks, and runtime guards.\n- Autoreview: clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Regression coverage verifies primary and queued follow-up channel paths, full start/update/end propagation, successful final payload delivery, and the same-name catalog-tool collision case.\n",
        "branch": "fix/hide-code-mode-wait-progress",
